title: 'cumulus: buffer session-based config items in RelayChainDataCache'

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      The slot-based Aura collator previously re-queried relay-chain configuration items that are
      constant within a session (`scheduling_lookahead`, `max_relay_parent_session_age`,
      `node_features` and `max_pov_size`) on every block-building iteration, issuing one relay
      runtime call per item per relay block — including for ancestor blocks that are only walked
      while finding the relay parent.

      These items are now buffered per session in `RelayChainDataCache`. A new `SessionData`
      struct holds the session-constant configuration, cached keyed by `SessionIndex`, while the
      per-relay-block `RelayChainData` keeps only genuinely per-block data (`relay_header`,
      `claim_queue`, `session_index`). 

crates:
  - name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
    bump: minor
  - name: cumulus-client-consensus-common
    bump: major
